            <ArticleTitle>A 58-Year-Old Female with Progressive Cough and Right Shoulder Pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>3049298</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Cavitary pneumonia in immunocompromised patients is a challenging entity. Establishing accurate diagnosis and starting effective antibiotics are essential steps towards improving outcome. A 58-year-old stem cell transplant patient was admitted to the hospital with necrotizing pneumonia caused by nocardia. The disease progressed despite of aggrieve antimicrobial therapy. Nocardiosis continues to be a difficult disease to diagnose and treat.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
